 "text": "With Black just cut in at F3, Opus 5.5 played E4 and lost 3.9 points, its worst move of the game. Black's lead went from +2.7 to +6.6, while the engine's choice was B8 on the left edge."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "Black's E1 was the game's one blunder, losing 8.4 points. The lead swung from +6.4 to -2.0, putting White ahead for the only time. The engine's choice was B8, the same point it had been suggesting since turn 17."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "Opus 5.5 played B8 at once, but the move lost 2.1 points and the lead went from -2.0 back to +0.1 for Black. The edge fight around the C-file wall was still open, and White had not yet taken the lead."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "B9 lost 2.5 points, moving the lead from +0.1 to +2.5, with the engine preferring C9. Black took C9 on the next move and kept a 2.5-point lead through to the end, where the final result was B+2."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberty count with a danger flag, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally area score with named dead stones removed. Both only inspect the current position and never generate, rank or look ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}